From 08c66533cbf8abbe6c36f29dfda017ff5a747632 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 08:34:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: pci: add Intel Meteor Lake xDCI 0x7ec2

The HP Meteor Lake laptop this tree targets exposes a USB device controller
that dwc3-pci does not claim, so the machine cannot act as a USB peripheral
and USB adb is impossible on it.

The controller is there and firmware has it enabled. PCI enumeration shows two
USB functions on the same device:

    0000:00:0d.0 [8086:7ec0] class 0x0c0330   xHCI, host
    0000:00:0d.2 [8086:7ec2] class 0x0c0340   USB device controller

Class 0c0340 is a USB device controller rather than a host one, so this is
xDCI. Nothing binds to it: dwc3-pci carries MTL 0x7e7e, MTLM 0x7eb1,
MTLP 0x7ec1 and MTLS 0x7f6f, and 0x7ec2 appears nowhere in the tree. The
driver is built and simply never matches, which looks identical to the
hardware not existing -- dmesg mentions dwc3 zero times either way.

Add the ID next to the other Meteor Lake entries, using the same
dwc3_pci_intel_swnode as MTLP, which is the adjacent function on the same
device and the closest existing match.

Signed-off-by: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-pci.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-pci.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-pci.c
index 6c1cbb722ca8..dcbb3fa9c062 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-pci.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-pci.c
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@
 #define PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_ADLS		0x7ae1
 #define PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_MTLM		0x7eb1
 #define PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_MTLP		0x7ec1
+#define PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_MTLP2		0x7ec2
 #define PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_MTLS		0x7f6f
 #define PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TGL			0x9a15
 #define PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_SPTLP		0x9d30
@@ -438,6 +439,7 @@ static const struct pci_device_id dwc3_pci_id_table[] = {
 	{ PCI_DEVICE_DATA(INTEL, ADLS, &dwc3_pci_intel_swnode) },
 	{ PCI_DEVICE_DATA(INTEL, MTLM, &dwc3_pci_intel_swnode) },
 	{ PCI_DEVICE_DATA(INTEL, MTLP, &dwc3_pci_intel_swnode) },
+	{ PCI_DEVICE_DATA(INTEL, MTLP2, &dwc3_pci_intel_swnode) },
 	{ PCI_DEVICE_DATA(INTEL, MTLS, &dwc3_pci_intel_swnode) },
 	{ PCI_DEVICE_DATA(INTEL, TGL, &dwc3_pci_intel_swnode) },
 	{ PCI_DEVICE_DATA(INTEL, SPTLP, &dwc3_pci_intel_swnode) },
-- 
